      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 99 and 99, we can use the standard multiplication method or recognize a pattern that simplifies the calculation. Let's go through the steps in detail.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's use the standard multiplication method:\n1. Multiply 99 by 9 (the units digit of 99):\n   99 \u00d7 9 = 891\n2. Multiply 99 by 90 (the tens digit of 99, which is 9 \u00d7 10):\n   99 \u00d7 90 = 8910\n3. Add the two results together:\n   891 + 8910 = 9801\nAlternatively, we can recognize that 99 is 100 - 1. Therefore, we can use the difference of squares formula:\n(100 - 1) \u00d7 (100 - 1) = 100\u00b2 - 2 \u00d7 100 + 1\u00b2 = 10000 - 200 + 1 = 9801\nBoth methods yield the same result, confirming that the product of 99 and 99 is 9801.\n</answer>",
