      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 73 and 74, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. Specifically, we can express 74 as 73 + 1. Therefore, the product of 73 and 74 can be written as:\n\\[ 73 \\times 74 = 73 \\times (73 + 1) \\]\nUsing the distributive property, we can expand this expression:\n\\[ 73 \\times (73 + 1) = 73 \\times 73 + 73 \\times 1 \\]\nSince \\( 73 \\times 1 = 73 \\), the expression simplifies to:\n\\[ 73 \\times 73 + 73 \\]\nNow, we need to calculate \\( 73 \\times 73 \\). We can use the formula for the square of a binomial, \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\), where \\( a = 70 \\) and \\( b = 3 \\):\n\\[ 73^2 = (70 + 3)^2 = 70^2 + 2 \\times 70 \\times 3 + 3^2 \\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[ 70^2 = 4900 \\]\n\\[ 2 \\times 70 \\times 3 = 420 \\]\n\\[ 3^2 = 9 \\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[ 73^2 = 4900 + 420 + 9 = 5329 \\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[ 73 \\times 73 = 5329 \\]\nSubstituting this back into our expression:\n\\[ 73 \\times 74 = 5329 + 73 \\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[ 5329 + 73 = 5402 \\]\nTherefore, the product of 73 and 74 is 5402.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 73 and 74 is 5402.\n</answer>",
